/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate22_vp_diNButylEther -- the vapour pressure of diNButylEther, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 step 2).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  diNButylEther`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION, committed
  before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1016/j.fluid.2006.06.017      26 pts  346.03-413.67 K  Lladosa; Monton; Burguet; Munoz
      10.1016/j.fluid.2015.05.002      14 pts  430.15-508.15 K  Liebergesell; Kaminski; Pauls; de Loos et al.
      10.1016/j.fluid.2007.09.002      10 pts  263.15-343.15 K  Boukais-Belaribi; Belaribi; Lohmann; Jose
      10.1021/je7007523                 7 pts  313.15-313.15 K  Alonso-Tristan; Villamanan; Chamorro; Segovia
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1016/j.fluid.2005.06.017: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1016/j.fluid.2005.11.026: 3 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1016/j.fluid.2012.01.008: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/acs.jced.7b00119: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/je060237w: 4 pressure point(s), fewer than 5
      10.1021/je100019r: 3 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1016/j.fluid.2006.06.017 (26 pts, 346.03-413.67 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1016/j.fluid.2015.05.002 (14 pts,
  430.15-508.15 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 0.36 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 14 points (0.171 to 0.629 %, mean 0.3574 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 415.35 K lies INSIDE the measured span 346.03-508.15 K: the held-out verdict is the test there, no further condition.

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  (filled in by bin/choupo-curate after the run)
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  diNButylEther;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/diNButylEther-vapourPressure-j.fluid.2006.06.017.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.fluid.2006.06.017"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/diNButylEther-vapourPressure-j.fluid.2015.05.002.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.fluid.2015.05.002"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  0.36 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 14 points (0.171 to 0.629 %, mean 0.3574 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
